WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.194 --> 00:00:02.694
(piano music)

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.978
- I sort of fell in love with the country,

00:00:05.978 --> 00:00:10.046
with the people, with the
idea of the revival of

00:00:10.046 --> 00:00:14.115
a Jewish community in
the country of Ukraine.

00:00:14.115 --> 00:00:16.034
And I decided that this
is where I wanna be.

00:00:16.034 --> 00:00:19.219
I wanna stay here and open a bakery.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:22.017
My name is Aaron Levitz,
I'm a baker from New York

00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:24.453
living in Uzhhorod, Ukraine.

00:00:24.453 --> 00:00:26.953
(piano music)

00:00:39.896 --> 00:00:43.263
I met my wife when I was in
culinary school in New York

00:00:43.263 --> 00:00:47.430
and she's from Ukraine so we
decided to move to Ukraine.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.685
I can't really sit in New York,

00:00:51.685 --> 00:00:53.510
where everything is Jewishly comfortable

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:56.365
when I know that in Ukraine,
things are difficult.

00:00:56.365 --> 00:00:58.475
I feel that I have a larger connection

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.558
with the Jews of Ukraine.

00:01:03.203 --> 00:01:04.704
Jewish life in Uzhhorod before the war

00:01:04.704 --> 00:01:07.787
compared to today is a huge contrast.

00:01:08.861 --> 00:01:12.608
Before the war you had many
synagogues, many rabbis.

00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:15.785
The Nazis came and they shipped
everyone out to Auschwitz

00:01:15.785 --> 00:01:18.882
and now there's no real community.

00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:21.382
(chime music)

00:01:22.676 --> 00:01:25.108
My part now in the Jewish community

00:01:25.108 --> 00:01:27.680
is to make an attempt at a Jewish revival

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.347
and so we're starting with food.

00:01:31.273 --> 00:01:32.724
It's not really practical to make

00:01:32.724 --> 00:01:35.819
a kosher bakery in Ukraine
or in Uzhhorod just for Jews,

00:01:35.819 --> 00:01:36.891
you're not really gonna make any money

00:01:36.891 --> 00:01:38.294
cause there's not enough Jews,

00:01:38.294 --> 00:01:41.246
so that's why I wanna introduce new ideas,

00:01:41.246 --> 00:01:44.331
new American pastries, Jewish pasteries

00:01:44.331 --> 00:01:45.923
that are just not common here, so,

00:01:45.923 --> 00:01:49.245
try to get the interest of people.

00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:50.745
I would say that I'm introducing some

00:01:50.745 --> 00:01:54.580
Jewish and American foods
that are non-judgmental.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.734
Some people are scared
to go to a synagogue

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:59.306
or scared to go to a
prayer service or something

00:01:59.306 --> 00:02:00.809
but they'll come into a bakery

00:02:00.809 --> 00:02:03.476
and have something tasty to eat.

